Step 3: Update Stop() to drain with 10s deadline

Replace `Stop()` (lines 213-218) with:
```go
func (e *Engine) Stop() {
    e.stopped.Store(true)
    if e.cancel != nil {
        e.cancel()
    }
    done := make(chan struct{})
    go func() {
        e.wg.Wait()
        close(done)
    }()
    select {
    case <-done:
    case <-time.After(10 * time.Second):
        logging.Warn("scheduler", "graceful shutdown deadline exceeded, some handlers still in-flight")
    }
}
```
Note: `stopped` is set BEFORE cancel so new packets are rejected immediately. `wg.Wait()` then drains in-flight ones.
